  {
   "title": "",
   "mode": "action",
   "sentences": [
    "Just after midnight on 30 July 1945, two torpedoes struck the American heavy cruiser USS Indianapolis.",
    "Twelve minutes later, she rolled over and sank into the dark Philippine Sea.",
    "About 300 men went down with her.",
    "The rest were left floating in the open ocean, with few lifeboats and almost no food or water.",
    "Only days earlier, this same ship had delivered the heart of the first atomic bomb used in war.",
    "And yet, for almost four days, nobody in the Navy noticed that she was gone.",
    "This is the story of the men in the water, the submarine that found them, and the captain who was blamed for all of it."
   ],
