   "title": "The Flagship",
   "mode": "action",
   "sentences": [
    "Indianapolis was launched in 1931, a Portland-class heavy cruiser named after the city of Indianapolis, Indiana.",
    "She carried nine big guns in three turrets, and two catapults for her own aircraft.",
    "From 1943 to 1945, she was the flagship of Admiral Raymond Spruance, who commanded the Fifth Fleet across the Central Pacific.",
    "She shelled the beaches of Saipan, and in February 1945 she covered the landings on Iwo Jima.",
    "On 31 March 1945, off Okinawa, a Japanese fighter dived straight at her bridge.",
    "The pilot released his bomb from just 25 feet, then crashed into the sea.",
    "The bomb went down through the deck, the mess hall and the fuel tanks, and exploded under the keel, killing nine crewmen.",
    "Badly damaged, Indianapolis steamed under her own power all the way to the Mare Island Naval Shipyard in California.",
    "It was there, freshly repaired, that she received the most secret orders of the war."
   ],
