  {
   "title": "The Hunter",
   "mode": "people",
   "sentences": [
    "Far to the north, in Kure, a Japanese submarine was getting ready for another patrol.",
    "She was I-58, and her captain was Lieutenant Commander Mochitsura Hashimoto.",
    "Hashimoto was born in Kyoto, the son of a Shinto priest.",
    "In 1941, he had been aboard the submarine I-24 during the attack on Pearl Harbor.",
    "Now his boat was one of only four large submarines Japan had left.",
    "She was equipped to carry kaiten, manned torpedoes, as well as ordinary ones.",
    "On 27 July, Hashimoto reached the shipping lane between Guam and Leyte.",
    "Indianapolis left Guam the next day, heading for Leyte along that same lane.",
    "McVay had asked for a destroyer escort, but his request was denied.",
    "Just six days earlier, Japanese submarines had sunk the destroyer Underhill in that area, yet McVay was never told.",
    "He was warned that Japanese submarines might be there, but not of any confirmed activity.",
    "His orders were to zigzag at his discretion, weather permitting.",
    "That night, with no escort, she was steaming at 17 knots in poor visibility."
   ],
