  {
   "title": "Twelve Minutes",
   "mode": "action",
   "sentences": [
    "At 23:35 on 29 July, Hashimoto spotted a large ship heading towards him.",
    "With the moon behind him, he took her for an Idaho-class battleship.",
    "He dived, let her come closer, and fired six torpedoes.",
    "Minutes later, two of them struck her starboard side, one in the bow and one amidships.",
    "The first tore away more than forty feet of her bow, and the second hit below the bridge.",
    "Top-heavy from all the guns added during the war, she listed hard and settled by the bow.",
    "Her radio operators keyed distress calls as she went down.",
    "Twelve minutes after the torpedoes hit, Indianapolis rolled completely over, lifted her stern into the air, and sank.",
    "Of the 1,195 men aboard, some 300 went down with her.",
    "McVay was one of the last to abandon ship.",
    "Hashimoto dived deep to reload, and when he came back up an hour later, she was gone.",
    "He radioed his headquarters that the ship had been destroyed, and turned for home."
   ],
