  {
   "title": "Four Days in the Water",
   "mode": "people",
   "sentences": [
    "There were few lifeboats, and many of the men had no life jackets at all.",
    "By day, the hot sun burned them, and at night they shook with cold.",
    "Salt water and fuel oil burned and peeled their skin.",
    "Some found Spam and crackers floating among the wreckage, but there was almost no fresh water.",
    "Men who drank sea water became delirious, and some began to see things that were not there.",
    "Then came the sharks.",
    "Hundreds of them were drawn to the wreck, and they began attacking the survivors.",
    "Estimates of the men killed by sharks run from a few dozen to 150.",
    "One documentary called it the most shark attacks on humans in history.",
    "Yet most of those who died were killed by exposure, salt water and thirst."
   ],
