  {
   "title": "The Rescue",
   "mode": "action",
   "sentences": [
    "On the morning of 2 August, a Navy PV-1 Ventura was flying a routine patrol over the area.",
    "Its pilot, Lieutenant Wilbur Gwinn, looked down and spotted men adrift in the water.",
    "He radioed his base on Peleliu and dropped a life raft and a radio, and every unit that could help was sent at once.",
    "His commanding officer, Lieutenant Richard Atteberry, flew out to circle the area and guide the others in.",
    "Next came a PBY Catalina flying boat, flown by Lieutenant Commander Robert Adrian Marks.",
    "Standing orders forbade landing in the open ocean.",
    "Marks took a vote of his crew, and they decided to land anyway, in twelve-foot swells.",
    "He was able to manoeuvre his aircraft to pick up 56 survivors.",
    "When there was no more room inside, he had men lashed to the wings with parachute cord.",
    "The landing left the plane unable to fly.",
    "After nightfall, the destroyer escort Cecil J. Doyle arrived, and used its searchlight as a beacon.",
    "For the men still in the water, it was the first sign of hope.",
    "Doyle and six other ships picked up the remaining survivors.",
    "Of the 890 men who had been set adrift, only 316 survived.",
    "No American warship sunk at sea has ever lost more sailors."
   ],
